DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       This program generates an index image in PPM format  for  a  photo  CD,
       based on the photo CD overview file.

       You  can  achieve a similar result with hhppccddttooppppmm --OOvveerrvviieeww followed by
       ppnnmmiinnddeexx --bbllaacckk on the generated PPM images.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppccddoovvttooppppmm recognizes the
       following command line options:



       --ww_w_i_d_t_h
              Maximum width of the result image (default: 1152).

       --ss_s_i_z_e Maximum size of each of the images (default: 192).

       --aa_a_c_r_o_s_s
              Maximum number of images across (default: 6).

       --cc_c_o_l_o_r_s
              Maximum number of colors, or nn

              to mean no quantization

       --ff_f_o_n_t Font to be used for annotation (default: internal font).

       --bb     Black background color (default).

       --ww     White background color.



       The Netpbm common options --vveerrssiioonn, --ppllaaiinn and --qquuiieett were  implemented
       starting with Netpbm 10.91 (June 2020).  Before that, none of these op‐
       tions were valid.



